    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0161" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/1401: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-24">March 24, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1072. Your airgram A–415, March 6;<anchor n="58" xml:id="d143-f1"/> and telegram
                    1347, March 18, 1943.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d143-f2"/> Board of Economic Warfare
                    concurs in final draft of memorandum.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d143-f3"/> You may
                    formalize this agreement by an exchange of notes with the Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d143-f1" n="58" xml:id="d143-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it indicated that export controls from the United States to Brazil
                    would be decentralized so that the Carteira de Exportação e Importação of the
                    Bank of Brazil would make the recommendations on export preference requests upon
                    proof that orders had been accepted by American firms (832.24/1384).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d143-f2" n="59" xml:id="d143-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d143-f3" n="59" xml:id="d143-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
